{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":242526,"duration_api_ms":242476,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture:** `cmd/` (per-utility binaries), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscalls), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `docs/` (specs/PRDs), `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded — not a generation target).\n\n**Implementation state (from source_code):** All packages with code in source_code already exist: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/du`, `cmd/ls`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/version`. This covers releases 00.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3, 03.0, 04.0, 04.1.\n\n**Current release:** rel02.0 (Batch 2 — trivial utilities: true, false, yes, basename, dirname) is the earliest incomplete release. All five use cases have `specstatus: pending` — no PRDs, use cases, or test suites exist yet. Per P5 (PRDs before use cases before test suites before code), the PRDs must be written first.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is rel02.0. All spec-complete releases already have code in source_code. The remaining releases (02.0, 02.1, 02.2) all have pending specs. Per P5 and P8, documentation tasks come before code, and PRDs come before everything else. The first two use cases in rel02.0 are `rel02.0-uc001-true` and `rel02.0-uc002-false` — both are trivially simple utilities (exit 0 / exit 1) and natural candidates for combining per P2.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Write PRDs for true and false utilities (rel02.0-uc001, rel02.0-uc002)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: documentation\n    format_rule: prd-format\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd005-wc.yaml (PRD format and structure reference)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (PRD format and structure reference)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (project structure, naming conventions, design decisions)\n      - docs/VISION.yaml (project goals, success criteria, scope boundaries)\n\n    files:\n      - path: docs/specs/product-requirements/prd012-true.yaml\n        action: create\n        note: PRD for the true utility\n      - path: docs/specs/product-requirements/prd013-false.yaml\n        action: create\n        note: PRD for the false utility\n\n    required_sections:\n      - \"Problem: why a formal specification is needed for this utility\"\n      - \"Goals: numbered goals (G1, G2, ...)\"\n      - \"Requirements: numbered requirements (R1.1, R1.2, ...) covering all flags, exit codes, and stream behaviors\"\n      - \"Non-Goals: what is out of scope for this utility\"\n      - \"Acceptance Criteria: checkable outcomes matching requirements\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Write a complete PRD for the true utility (prd012-true.yaml). The PRD\n          must cover: unconditional exit with code 0, --help flag printing usage\n          to stdout and exiting 0, --version flag printing version string to stdout\n          and exiting 0, SIGPIPE signal handling (exit cleanly), and the fact that\n          true reads no stdin and produces no stdout in normal operation.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Write a complete PRD for the false utility (prd013-false.yaml). The PRD\n          must cover: unconditional exit with code 1, --help flag printing usage\n          to stdout and exiting 0, --version flag printing version string to stdout\n          and exiting 0, SIGPIPE signal handling (exit cleanly), and the fact that\n          false reads no stdin and produces no stdout in normal operation.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Both PRDs must follow the existing PRD format used by prd005-wc.yaml and\n          prd006-cat.yaml. Requirements must be numbered (R1.1, R1.2, ...) and\n          acceptance criteria must be checkable and map to requirements. Goals must\n          be numbered (G1, G2, ...).\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Use the same YAML PRD format structure as existing PRDs in the project.\n          Read prd005-wc.yaml or prd006-cat.yaml first to establish the format,\n          then create new PRDs matching that structure exactly.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          true and false are the two simplest GNU coreutils utilities. Their PRDs\n          should be minimal but complete -- covering exit code, flag handling\n          (--help, --version), signal handling (SIGPIPE), and explicitly stating\n          that no stdin/stdout I/O occurs in normal operation.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          The reference binaries for differential testing are gtrue and gfalse\n          (Homebrew GNU coreutils with g- prefix). Note this in the PRD so the\n          test suite and implementation know which reference binary to use.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: docs/specs/product-requirements/prd012-true.yaml exists and contains all required sections (Problem, Goals, Requirements, Non-Goals, Acceptance Criteria)\n      - id: AC2\n        text: docs/specs/product-requirements/prd013-false.yaml exists and contains all required sections (Problem, Goals, Requirements, Non-Goals, Acceptance Criteria)\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All requirements in both PRDs are numbered (R1.1, R1.2, ...) and specific enough to implement without ambiguity\n      - id: AC4\n        text: All acceptance criteria in both PRDs are checkable outcomes that map to specific requirements\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Both PRDs identify the correct GNU reference binary name (gtrue, gfalse) for differential testing\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"8e3c14cd-22a9-4fd7-ad54-4ddc799de152","total_cost_usd":0.903667,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":89722,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"output_tokens":13330,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":89722,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13330,"cacheReadInputTokens":19289,"cacheCreationInputTokens":89722,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.903667,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"b8fe9ceb-b647-4c58-991d-6e4320e14b6f"}
